CORE
main.cpp
--cpp14
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ generic lambda capturing this: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [expr.prim.lambda.closure]/4: a generic lambda passed to a function
template is called with a double; its call operator is instantiated for
double.  The function-pointer lowering made the lambda an `int (*)(int &)'
in a member function, so fmt<int> was instantiated and dropped and the
result was wrong (bin53).  See cpp14_generic_lambda_by_reference_capture.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program (-std=c++14), and it fails only
its WRONG assertion.
